  Repository coverage and compiled/live CLI acceptance passed after transport/resource integration.,"bun run test:coverage && bun run test:e2e && SEARXNG_URL=http://192.168.1.183:38522 bun run test:e2e:searxng",100/100/100/100 across 962 tests; 62 black-box E2E tests; installed searxng live suite passes GET/POST/RSS/resources/contracts.
  Release-ready acceptance passed at version 2026.7.31.,"bun run release:check && bun run security:trivy && bun run secrets:history && bun run smoke:package",962 tests and 100/100/100/100; 21 built-in live tests; isolated installed CLI; zero HIGH/CRITICAL findings; clean history scan; npm and Bun consumer aliases.
plan_decisions[2]{ts,author,decision,rationale,evidence}:
  "2026-07-31T20:21:44.789Z",codex-searxng-20260731,Add POST as an explicit search transport while retaining GET as the compatibility default; normalize both through the existing JSON-first and HTML-fallback pipeline.,"Official SearXNG supports both methods, GET preserves compatibility, and form-encoded POST avoids URL-length exposure for larger parameter sets.",Official docs/dev/search_api.rst at master 6bfd827; live 2026.7.31 service; src/search/index.ts currently GET-only.
  "2026-07-31T20:55:36.219Z",codex-searxng-20260731,"Authenticate optional OpenMetrics through environment variables, never persistent settings or request diagnostics, and accept typed 401/404 capability evidence in live release checks.",The upstream API is administrative and secret-backed; environment injection prevents durable credential exposure while preserving full enabled-endpoint support.,Official settings_general open_metrics contract and live /metrics 404 acceptance.
plan_discoveries[2]{ts,author,text}:
  "2026-07-31T20:55:35.562Z",codex-searxng-20260731,The live 2026.7.31 service returns HTTP 404 for /metrics because SearXNG general.open_metrics is disabled by default; official current docs require a configured secret and HTTP Basic authentication when enabled.
  "2026-07-31T21:02:36.682Z",codex-searxng-20260731,The release gate parsed typed instance stats/errors as legacy top-level fields even though the CLI contract has always wrapped resource data under .data; live release acceptance exposed and corrected those assertions.
